{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102574-oh-it-s-just-a-yantra","id":1102574,"title":"Oh, It's just a Yantra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-11T12:19:41-07:00","id":1102574,"title":"Oh, It's just a Yantra","content":"For some reason the phrase &quot;Oh, It's just a Yantra&quot; has become a staple of almost every game session. It is often used as a way for mages (both PCs and NPCs) to get a free pass on some questionable or odd behavior (occasionally you can instead use &quot;It's just an Oblation&quot; to spice things up). Examples:<br /> <br /> Why do you have a noose hanging in the middle of the living room? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why are did you buy these 10 galons of pig blood for? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why are you having sex with a stranger on my bed? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why are you drowning your cabal mate in the tub? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why do you have so many jars full of water from rivers all around the world stored in this closet? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why are we robbing this old flag from the museum? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why did you walk into my room without knocking first while covered in spiders? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Why have you spent the last two weeks playing online video games? It's just a Yantra.<br /> <br /> <br /> True examples by the way. Any weird stuff your Mages do while using the Yantra / Oblation excuse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:14:14-07:00","id":1103330,"title":"","content":"Our resident Libertine's techne is based on people around him texting in 'jejemon', a subculture in the Philippines that subverts the English language, and turns it into something almost incomprehensible when texting. In a sense, a new language. <br /> <br /> Normal laughing on SMS: hehehehehe<br /> Jejemon laughing on SMS: jejejejejeje<br /> <br /> In the real world, it's quite annoying. In-game, I find it hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:51:11-07:00","id":1103467,"title":"","content":"It would also be fun to come up with some kind of crazy Yantra/Oblation and then try to figure out what kind of spell/legacy it would be used for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:30:26-07:00","id":1106095,"title":"","content":"Huh. You know, I don't think my players have ever tried anything unusual as yantra. Maybe I just have boring players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:37:24-07:00","id":1106132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102574-oh-it-s-just-a-yantra?p=1106095#post1106095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I just have boring players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:44:46-07:00","id":1106135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102574-oh-it-s-just-a-yantra?p=1106132#post1106132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, boring is a bit too harsh. Could be many reasons to not pursue unusual lines of thinking in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:58:53-07:00","id":1106145,"title":"","content":"I think most games don't bring up unusual Yantras because they're often not that good, and most player characters don't have enough Yantra slots to fill with more than the most common Yantras. Mudra, Persona, Mantra and demesne are great yantras. The first two can exceed 2 dice while Mantra is universal and demesne will fit the spells that you normally tend to cast. If you most of the time manage to incorporate at least three of those four Yantras in your spells (which, in my experience, is common) then you're able to routinely fill all your Yantra slots from Gnosis 1 to Gnosis 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:01:50-07:00","id":1106148,"title":"","content":"Plus, there's only a limited number of things that can be a Yantra anyway, and most of them aren't unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:48:30-07:00","id":1106699,"title":"","content":"I always throw them at least a little extra +1 if the Yantra is particularly interesting. <br /> <br /> Also, lately I have been experimenting with removing the Gnosis-based limit to Yantras and its working fine (but I have a bunch of other things to balance that out, so YMMV).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:30:47-07:00","id":1106848,"title":"","content":"I had a thought, back in first edition before talk of Yantras became public, of allowing a Mage to use the Occult skill to create a pentagram (like a summoning circle) that would allow them to stack additional tools to ward off Paradox (a cup on one point, mirror on another and coin on a third etc...) in a ritual casting. This would boost the value of a secure sanctum as a properly drawn and kept circle could be used over and over again. It would also add to the value of a mentor or more advanced Mage as they could loan out their circles to lesser Mages to use. If desired the ST could require a different circle for different Arcanum combinations, necessitating the keeping of multiple such in a sanctum.<br /> \u200bYou could also give equipment bonuses on the creation of the circle for using valuable or hard to find materials, such as gold, silver or ground cryptid bones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T22:10:42-07:00","id":1106877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102574-oh-it-s-just-a-yantra?p=1106699#post1106699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always throw them at least a little extra +1 if the Yantra is particularly interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains your different experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T04:27:10-07:00","id":1106955,"title":"","content":"One time my players snuck into a hospital and used a Life Ruling spell to siphon the blood out of a bunch of babies in order to collect it in vials. They stole the blood from an entire ward so that they didn't kill any of the infants.<br /> <br /> Reason? A rampaging spirit of violent murder could be harmed by a weapon coated in the blood of innocents...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure they've ever specifically sought out weird Yantras, but I feel that one is in the same vein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T04:38:25-07:00","id":1106961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102574-oh-it-s-just-a-yantra?p=1106877#post1106877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explains your different experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely, that's already the rule for Sacraments whch at least some of the examples look like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}